+# The contract the logger emits against is one it can satisfy
+
+Status: ready-for-agent
+
+Blocks: 05, which cannot report a rate until this lands.
+
+The first pass of `trainer eval --suite log` against the graph held **24 of 90**
+on `gpt-oss:20b`. Rescored on the document the engine would *write* --
+`log.to_performed` of what was emitted -- the 50 determined runs that produced a
+document go from **7 to 30** held. Most of what failed is the contract the model
+emits against, not its reading of the report.
+
+**Read first**: `docs/logging/eval-set.md` -- how to read a row, U1, U2, U16;
+`coach/logger.py` -- `LOGGING` and `validate`; `coach/planner.py` --
+`validate`, `FEEDBACK`, `_emit_schema`; `log.py` -- `validate` and
+`to_performed`; `log_evaluation.py` -- `score` and `_notes`.
+
+## What the pass found
+
+| # | the contract says | and |
+|---|---|---|
+| 1 | every value in a block is required (`strict_schema(PerformedWorkout)`) | `LOGGING` forbids `assumed` and says a value nobody gave is left out |
+| 2 | a refused document ends the run (`validate` to `END`, `REFUSED`) | the planner's refusal goes back to the model, three attempts |
+| 3 | an exclusion names a pattern or a joint | neither vocabulary is anywhere in the context |
+
+## What to build
+
+- **Provenance as the shape allows.** A report of *"solo 2 serie di militari"*
+  forces a block whose `amount` and `rest` the user never gave; the prompt
+  leaves no legal way to write it, and U2 and U16 expect exactly the prescribed
+  number labelled `assumed`. The rule to say is the one `log.validate` already
+  enforces: **a block the report forces open carries the prescription's own
+  numbers, labelled `assumed`; a block the report does not touch is left out
+  entirely** and adherence fills it in.
+  `_nothing_assumed_the_prescription_does_not_say` refuses only a
+  *contradiction*, so this is the prompt catching up with the validator and not
+  a new licence. U1 is unmoved: nothing deviated, so `blocks` is still empty.
+- **A refusal goes back to the model, bounded.** `planner.validate` is the
+  shape: an `attempts` count in `LoggerState`, what `log.parse` or
+  `log.validate` said sent back as a message, and an edge to `logger` -- not
+  straight to `emit`, because a wrong id is repaired by `search_exercises` and
+  not by thinking again. The run closes `REFUSED` only once the attempts are
+  spent.
+- **The refusals in the shape the record reads.** `record.of` builds `attempts`
+  from `state["refusals"]` and reads `.rule` and `.says` off each entry, which
+  is `plan.Violation`. The logger's refusals arrive in that shape or the
+  ADR-0007 document loses every attempt but the last; `LogError` and
+  `LogRejected` are the two rules, the way `plans.SHAPE` is one.
+- **The exclusion vocabulary, read from the data.** The only values a run ever
+  sees are the two examples in the prompt, and `KEEPS` carries neither
+  `movement_pattern` nor `loaded_joints`, so no tool result shows one either --
+  while U16 expects `lumbar spine`, the catalog's own value, with the space and
+  in lower case. `planner._emit_schema` is the precedent: hold
+  `proposed_exclusion.value` to an enum of `catalog.values(connection,
+  "movement_pattern")` plus `catalog.joint_values(connection)`. From the data,
+  never a constant.
+- **The two causes stay separable.** The rescore is what found all of this and
+  the suite cannot do it. Report it beside the number: how many determined runs
+  would hold if scored on the resolved document instead of the emitted one --
+  `_notes` is where a fact that is not a failure goes. **The score itself does
+  not move.** The set's U1 note calls restating the prescription the commonest
+  wrong answer, and 05 holds the invariants to the set's own rows.
+- **The pass runs against the fixture `TRAINER_DB` names**, which `prepared`
+  already does. The tools open their own connection, and the enum above is read
+  through one.
+
+## What this does not fix
+
+**The bar.** 30 of 50 is 60% with the contract discounted entirely, and the
+suite's bar is 100% and not a knob. Whatever is left once the contract is
+emittable is a finding about `gpt-oss:20b`, and ROADMAP.md § Risks names the
+fallbacks (`qwen3.5:9b`, `LLM_BACKEND=groq`). Which provider the suite is held
+at is 05's call, on its pass against both.
+
+**A document that never parses still lands in the `not run` column**, beside an
+unreachable provider. It counts against the metric either way -- `Outcome.held`
+is false for both -- so it is a label and not an arithmetic error, and with
+attempts in front of it, it should be rare. Four of the 54 determined runs
+ended there.
+
+## Acceptance criteria
+
+- [ ] A report that deviates on rounds alone emits one block whose `amount` and
+      `rest` are `assumed` at the prescribed values, and `log.validate` passes
+      it. Watched happen on U2 and U16, not read off the code.
+- [ ] A refused document comes back to the model with what the validator said,
+      and a run that repairs it reaches `DONE` with the record's `attempts`
+      saying there were two.
+- [ ] A run refused to the end still closes `REFUSED`, as it does today.
+- [ ] `proposed_exclusion.value` cannot be emitted outside the catalog's own
+      patterns and joints.
+- [ ] `trainer eval --suite log` re-run on the same provider, the number
+      reported before and after, and no run in the matrix failing for a
+      provenance the shape forced, a first refusal, or an exclusion value
+      outside the vocabulary.
+- [ ] Every failure left is named per row as a failure of the reading.
+- [ ] The full test suite and mypy are green.
+
+## Comments
+
+Found by the first pass on the graph, 2026-09-22. The prompt's provenance
+section was written against a shape that let a value be omitted; nothing failed
+when `strict_schema` stopped allowing that, because the two have never been
+read side by side.
